    {
      "tension": "The state-of-the-art defense (sit-278): accelerationists want it preserved, skeptics note industry captures the standards that define it.",
      "opportunity": "Argue that the topic's tiering plus an 'independent, multi-disciplinary administrative board armed with federal subpoena power' converts a litigated, defendant-favorable defense into an ex ante certified tier with public criteria — conceding the capture_institutional critique and claiming the design fixes it. This buys credibility at low cost."
    },
    {
      "tension": "Acting now vs. waiting for proof (sit-019, sit-028): the accelerationist normally demands demonstrated harm before restriction, yet this proposal imposes mandatory pre-deployment standards and a tax now.",
      "opportunity": "Resolve it as proportional and evidence-generating: tiered obligations scale with domain severity, and the excise-funded oversight_audit plus telemetry is precisely the instrument that produces the evidence base both camps claim to want. Accelerationists can say they are funding the resolution of the empirical dispute rather than betting on either prior."
